<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russian Far East</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russian Far East is the easternmost part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, between eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a>, including the Amur and Primorye regions, Kamchatka, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakhalin">Sakhalin</a> and Chukotka. Russia acquired its southern parts from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a> by the treaties of Aigun in 1858 and Peking in 1860, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladivostok">Vladivostok</a> as its Pacific port. From 1903 a viceroyalty based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lushunkou">Port Arthur</a> briefly governed it together with the Kwantung lease.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russian-far-east.jpg" alt="Russian Far East" width="320" height="185" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Map of Russia - Far Eastern Federal District.svg: Lokal_Profil File:Map of Russian districts, 2018-11-04.svg: Fi... · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Russia_-_Far_Eastern_Federal_District_(2018_composition).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
